OL,3,AUnnamed celebrity accused of
OL,4,A'inappropriate sexual activities',
OL,5,Acourt hears
OL,6,
OL,7,FA trial has begun in which a celebrity
OL,8,Fis asking the High Court to prevent two
OL,9,Fnews organisations from publishing his
OL,10,Fidentity and allegations that he abused
OL,11,Fhis status for many years to engage, or
OL,12,Fattempt to engage, in "inappropriate
OL,13,Fsexual activities with a large number
OL,14,Fof girls and young women".
OL,16,FThe unnamed celebrity's legal team said
OL,17,Fany publication would "highly likely
OL,18,Flead him to commit suicide".
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
